  AGPL-3.0 (code) + CC BY-SA 4.0 (paper/data).
title: "The Sefirot Graph as Resonant Cavity: Spectral Theory of a 10-Node Governance Architecture"
abstract: >-
  Spectral analysis of a specific 10-node, 22-edge graph (sefirot graph)
  with Z2 pillar symmetry. Proves: Z2 parity decomposition into 7-dim even
  and 3-dim odd sectors with irreducible characteristic polynomials;
  Perron-Frobenius concentration of 86.7% at Tiferet (degree-8 hub),
  exceeding any Dynkin diagram or random graph; bimodal concentration with
  no intermediate weights; Z2-isospin isomorphism with exact dim V_minus
  = 3 = 2I+1; cross-coupling rank 3 = #Z2 pairs; Goldstone drop-by-2 as
  discrete GMOR analogue; complement duality lambda_bar_i = 10 - lambda_i;
  unique maximum equal-density bisection at 0.60; optimal Daat coupling
  (5-edge Tiferet-linked, w_c approx 1.7752). Applications to multi-agent
  governance with institutional convergence validation (Anthropic,
  Microsoft, Augment, IAIFI). Honest limitations stated: eigenvalue ratios
  do not match meson mass ratios; consciousness threshold is algebraically
  independent.
